# Search speed and show speed

Local search must feel instant: query fast, first results on screen fast.

- Search off the main thread; keep the UI thread free for rendering.
- Show the first useful results as soon as they are ready; do not wait for every source.
- Prefer incremental/partial updates over one big dump at the end.
- Index or cache what will be queried often (apps, recent queries); avoid full rescan on every keystroke.
- Debounce input, cancel stale queries, and ignore outdated results.
- Bind lists with stable IDs / payloads; do not rebuild the whole adapter on each keystroke.
- Measure query time and bind time when changing search or result UI.

```kotlin
// BAD: block UI, wait for all sources, then show
val all = sources.map { it.search(query) }.flatten()
adapter.submitList(all)

// GOOD: each source posts results as they finish; drop stale generations
```
